license: MIT
abstract: >-
  Lecture materials on machine learning interpretability for SCC5819 Topics
  in Artificial Intelligence, a graduate course at ICMC-USP taught by
  Prof. Andre Carlos Ponce de Leon Ferreira de Carvalho, following
  Christoph Molnar's Interpretable Machine Learning. Each module is a fully
  reproducible, real-data walkthrough on the Breast Cancer Wisconsin
  (Diagnostic) dataset, pairing a lecture notebook with a technical
  companion that measures the method's behaviour rather than restating its
  documentation. The modules share one model, one split and one patient, so
  they read as a single case: ceteris paribus profiles (01), individual
  conditional expectation curves (02), and LIME (03), the last including a
  line-by-line validation of the lime package internals.
